## Colour, part by part

No paint and no covers (rule of 2026-11-09): parts in brass, ivory, white or black, anything
sold only in another colour placed out of sight.

{md_tbl(["Part", "Colour as sold", "Where it sits", "What shows"], COLOURS)}

## Why these numbers

- 70 mm is the smallest sphere that takes the 27 mm screen below the equator and the 21 mm
  XIAO above it, 19 mm forward, with the 43 mm tray across the floor.
- The equator is a rod at y = 0, 14 mm in front of the boards: glass below it, lens above it,
  and the rod divides the face instead of crossing it.
- One 300 mm rod per big ring (220 mm around, 80 mm offcut); the base ring is a third rod.
- The posts are the screen's own mounting holes (about 23 mm pitch, measure it); the XIAO's
  short edges are glued to the same rods 0.5 mm away. No pin touches brass; the frame floats.
- The 11 mm gap behind the screen (board at z 17.8, tray wall at z 6.5) hides the 8 mm toggle
  body and the 3 mm amplifier, both above the screen's bottom edge and below the speaker's top.
- Cell at y = −19 puts 20 g of the 58 on the floor; it self-rights.
- The AHT20 sits 20 mm behind and 8 mm above the stack with open rods around it; expect 1–2 °C
  of self-heating offset after an hour of streaming, subtracted in firmware.

