## Risks

- The two big rings meet at a right angle at left and right: peg the side ring upright on a
  cardboard disc, tack one crossing, check square, tack the other.
- The screen's holes: if the module has none, or a pitch the posts cannot match, glue its edges
  as for the XIAO.
- The screen's board colour is the one open colour question; check it in the drawer.
- Wi-Fi: three rods with 35 mm gaps are no cage at 2.4 GHz; the antenna lies flat on the
  XIAO's back under Kapton, pointing up.
- Glue carries the XIAO: four dabs on a 0.5 mm gap; a day's cure before handling.
- A sphere rolls when knocked off its ring; the low cell brings it back. Test self-righting with
  the cell in before wiring.
